  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper experimentally evaluates QAOA for portfolio optimization (3–5 qubits) and MaxCut (5 qubits) on IBM superconducting QPUs (ibmq ehningen and ibm auckland) with up to p=5 layers and 50,000 shots per circuit. By exploiting pulse‑level optimized ZZ and ZZ‑SWAP gates on bipotent architectures, the authors report approximation‑ratio improvements of up to about 70% relative to fidelity‑only qubit mapping strategies. The work demonstrates that pulse‑level optimization and gate‑type selection can outperform circuits mapped solely for maximal gate fidelity on NISQ hardware.",
